  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Kebechet/Blazor.Swiper",
  "published": "2026-07-30T13:47:53.37Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING, and a much larger API. SwiperOptions now mirrors every one of Swiper's parameters - all 95 top-level ones plus the 22 nested module option records - and every member is nullable, so an unset member is the only signal for \"keep Swiper's default\". All 77 of Swiper's events now have a callback, subscribed only when you assign one, so an unwired event costs no listener and no interop. ActiveIndex is two-way bindable (@bind-ActiveIndex), as is IsAutoplayRunning. Options is now reactive: changing it pushes the members that moved to the live slider. Adds GetStateAsync, the full navigation and update method set, Autoplay/Zoom/Keyboard/Mousewheel/Slides/Virtual controllers, Thumbs and Controller cross-instance wiring, slide-level Zoom/Lazy/Hash/AutoplayDelay/VirtualIndex, per-slide state through SlideContent, declarative pagination templates, and EventThrottle for the events that fire per animation frame. Breaking: Direction is now the SwiperDirection enum (SwiperDirection.Horizontal still compiles, a literal \"horizontal\" does not); Pagination/Navigation/Scrollbar/Keyboard/Mousewheel are option records with an implicit conversion from bool, so `= true` still compiles; previously non-nullable options are nullable; SwiperSlide.ChildContent stays plain and per-slide state moved to SlideContent; the per-event JSInvokable methods collapsed into one dispatcher. Same vendored Swiper 14.0.6 bundle.",
